            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) in unstable angina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>9-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We performed percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty in 33 highly selected patients of unstable angina, a majority of whom were initially stabilized by medical therapy. All these patients had single vessel disease with type A lesion. The initial success rate was 91% with recurrence of 17% at the end of 1 year.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
